    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.sessions\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nwhen using **nui** to take over vim.ui.select (code like below 👇)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/MunifTanjim/nui.nvim/wiki/vim.ui#vimuiselect\r\n\r\nrequire('mini.sessions').select('read') will get a error 👇\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f78eba48-50e9-4c1f-b4d7-41708400292b)\r\n\r\nI read **the mini.sessions source code** and find the error maybe happen in 👇\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/903450f6-f492-465b-8e5c-4d5c643aa1bf)\r\n\r\nnui the error-related code maybe as follows 👇\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f7a640e-fbd9-4f58-a62c-aef04a226c24)\r\nand\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e72a278-b885-496f-82f0-bfdaee4b7476)\r\n\r\nBut I don't know the bug which is from nui code or mini.sessions\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.10\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. configure nui code (from https://github.com/MunifTanjim/nui.nvim/wiki/vim.ui#vimuiselect)\r\n2. configure mini.sessions to bind a keymap to `require('mini.sessions').select('read')`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nAn error occurred",
